<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Gjergj Thopia</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">d. <a href="/years/1392">1392</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/14th-century">14th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Gjergj Thopia was lord of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/durres">Durrës</a> and the last ruler of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/thopia-family">Thopia family</a>'s Principality of Albania, succeeding his father <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/karl-thopia">Karl Thopia</a> in 1388. Under Ottoman pressure he handed Durrës to <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/venice">Venice</a> in 1392, shortly before his death, and the rest of the Thopia lands later fell to the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ottoman-empire">Ottomans</a>.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/gjergj-thopia.jpg" alt="Gjergj Thopia" width="320" height="240" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Thesare të muzeut Historik kombëtar - Dorian Koçi and Andrea Llukani · CC BY 4.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Mbishkrimi_prej_mermeri_i_kish%C3%ABs_s%C3%AB_Sh%C3%ABn_Gjon_Vladimirit.png" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
